3	/// How a stored partial date relates to a query range.
4	///
5	/// The distinction exists because a coarse value denotes a *span*, not an
6	/// instant. "March 2019" is not the same claim as "1 March 2019, 00:00", and a
7	/// range query that treats it as the latter makes the record vanish from any
8	/// range that starts later in March. That is the failure this type prevents.
9	public enum RangeFit: String, Codable, Sendable, Hashable {
10	    /// Every instant the stored value could denote lies inside the range.
11	    case definite
12	    /// The span overlaps the range but also extends outside it, so the record
13	    /// *may* belong to the range. Returned and labelled, never dropped.
14	    case potential
15	}
